{{!
    @template local_extendednav/dialog/action

    The body of the question asked before an action on nodes: the tile of the action, what it does, its options (such as
    hiding from administrators too or blocking the address) as switches, the nodes the action leaves as they are (how many, and the first of
    them in a list that scrolls), and the place of the error if the action fails.

    @copyright  2026 Didactika.org
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Example context (json):
    {
        "icon": "t/hide", "tone": "secondary",
        "text": "The nodes are hidden from everyone they were shown to.",
        "switches": [{"id": "len-option", "key": "hideadmins", "label": "Hide from administrators too", "help": "Otherwise they keep seeing them.", "checked": true}],
        "skipped": {"text": "2 of the selected nodes are left as they are:", "names": ["Dashboard", "Site administration"], "more": ""}
    }
}}
<div class="d-flex align-items-start">
    <span class="icon-box text-{{tone}} mr-3 me-3">{{#pix}}{{icon}}, core{{/pix}}</span>
    <p class="mb-0">{{text}}</p>
</div>
{{#switches}}
    <div class="form-check form-switch custom-control custom-switch mt-3">
        <input type="checkbox" class="form-check-input custom-control-input" id="{{id}}" data-region="option" data-key="{{key}}" {{#checked}}checked{{/checked}}>
        <label class="form-check-label custom-control-label fw-bold" for="{{id}}">{{label}}</label>
        <p class="small text-muted mb-0">{{help}}</p>
    </div>
{{/switches}}
{{#skipped}}
    <div class="mt-3" data-region="skipped">
        <p class="small fw-bold mb-1">{{text}}</p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush border rounded overflow-auto small">
            {{#names}}<li class="list-group-item py-1">{{.}}</li>{{/names}}
            {{#more}}<li class="list-group-item py-1 text-muted">{{more}}</li>{{/more}}
        </ul>
    </div>
{{/skipped}}
<div class="alert alert-danger mt-3 mb-0" role="alert" data-region="confirm-error" hidden></div>
